</span></b>

<h2><a name="_Ref181506178"></a><a name="_Ref19084151"></a><a
name="_Toc189181951"></a><a name="_Ref188415023"><span lang=EN>3.7 </span><span
lang=EN>CommitResource </span></a><span lang=EN>Message</span></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181952"><span lang=EN>3.7.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “CommitResource” message is used by a
Resource Supplier to confirm that resources have been committed to a Resource
Consumer request. Usually, the CommitResource is in response to a RequisitionResource,
or even a RequestResource. The CommitResource is the only message used to
indicate the resources have been allocated to an assignment/incident.</span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181953"><span lang=EN>3.7.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 7<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the CommitResource Message. The </span><span
lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=487
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image008.jpg"></span></p>

<p class=MsoCaption><a name="_Ref153686916">Figure </a>7: EDXL-RM ERM for
CommitResource Message</p>

