<h2><a name="_Toc189181969"><span lang=EN>3.10 </span><span lang=EN>OfferUnsolicitedResource
Message</span></a></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181970"><span lang=EN>3.10.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “OfferUnsolicitedResource” message is used
to offer available resources (that have not been requested) to assist with an
emergency response.</span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181971"><span lang=EN>3.10.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 10<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the OfferUnsolicitedResource Message. The </span><span
lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=486
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image011.jpg"></span></p>

