<h2><a name="_Ref181507228"></a><a name="_Ref151456258"></a><a
name="_Toc189181981"></a><a name="_Ref188428527"><span lang=EN>3.12 </span><span
lang=EN>RequestReturn</span></a><span lang=EN> Message</span></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181982"><span lang=EN>3.12.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “RequestReturn” message is used to request
release (demobilization) of resource(s) back to its original owning
jurisdiction and location or to another location / assignment.</span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181983"><span lang=EN>3.12.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 12<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the RequestReturn Message. The </span><span
lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=486
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image013.jpg"></span></p>

<p class=MsoCaption><a name="_Ref153687547">Figure </a>12: EDXL-RM ERM for
RequestReturn Message</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>&nbsp;</span></p>

<span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><br clear=all
style='page-break-before:always'>
</span>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following table outlines the element cardinalities for
this message type.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=MsoCaption>Table 12: RequestReturn Message Elements </p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
