<h2><a name="_Ref181507131"></a><a name="_Toc189181987"></a><a
name="_Ref188427814"><span lang=EN>3.13 </span><span lang=EN>ResponseToRequestReturn
Message</span></a></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181988"><span lang=EN>3.13.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “ResponseToRequestReturn” message is used
by Resource Consumers to respond to a RequestReturn message from Resource Suppliers.
The response identifies the resources in the original request message and how
the Resource Consumer has responded.</span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181989"><span lang=EN>3.13.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 13<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the ResponseToRequestReturn Message. The </span><span
lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=486
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image014.jpg"></span></p>

<p class=MsoCaption><a name="_Ref153691055">Figure </a>13: EDXL-RM ERM for
ResponseToRequestReturn Message</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>&nbsp;</span></p>

<span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><br clear=all
style='page-break-before:always'>
</span>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following table outlines the element cardinalities for
this message type.</p>

