<h3><a name="_Toc189181990">3.13.3 ResponseToRequestReturn Message Rules</a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following rules apply to the above elements:</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The ResponseToRequestReturn:MessageID, ResponseToRequestReturn:SentDateTime,
ResponseToRequestReturn:MessageContentType, ResponseToRequestReturn:OriginatingMessageID,
ResponseToRequestReturn:PrecedingMessageID, ResponseToRequestReturn:ContactInformation,
and ResponseToRequestReturn:ResourceInformation elements MUST be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The value of ResponseToRequestReturn:MessageContentType MUST be “ResponseToRequestReturn”.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>If a ResponseToRequestReturn:IncidentInformation element is
present, then at least one of IncidentInformation:IncidentID and/or
IncidentInformation:IncidentDescription elements MUST be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>If the ResponseToRequestReturn:MessageRecall element is present,
then the MessageRecall:RecalledMessageID and MessageRecall:RecallType elements MUST
be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>If a ResponseToRequestReturn:Funding element is present, then at
least one of Funding:FundCode and/or Funding:FundingInfo elements MUST be
present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The ResourceInformation:ResourceInfoElementID and ResourceInformation:ResponseInformation
elements MUST be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The ResponseInformation:PrecedingResourceInfoElementID and ResponseInformation:ResponseType
elements MUST be present. </p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>If the ResponseInformation:ResponseType element has a value of “Provisional”,
then at least one of ResponseInformation:ReasonCode and/or ResponseInformation:ResponseReason
elements MUST be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>At least one of Resource:ResourceID, Resource:Name, and/or Resource:TypeStructure
elements MUST be present for each ResourceInformation:Resource element present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The Resource:ResourceStatus element MUST be present for each
ResourceInformation:Resource element present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>If a Resource:OwnershipInformation element is present, then at
least one of OwnershipInformation:Owner and/or
OwnershipInformation:OwningJurisdiction elements MUST be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The ResourceStatus:DeploymentStatus and
ResourceStatus:Availability elements MUST be present.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>If the ResourceInformation:ScheduleInformation element is
present, then the ScheduleInformation:ScheduleType element MUST be present and contain
one of the following values: </p>

<p class=MsoListBullet style='margin-left:.75in'><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>“RequestedArrival”, “EstimatedArrival”, “ActualArrival”,
“RequestedDeparture”, “EstimatedDeparture”, “ActualDeparture”, RequestedReturnArrival”,
“EstimatedReturnArrival”,” “BeginAvailable”, “RequestedReturnDeparture”,
“EstimatedReturnDeparture”, “ActualReturnDeparture”,  “EndAvailable”,
“Committed”, “Current”, “ReportTo”  or “Route.”</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The schema for a ResponseToRequestReturn message can be
found in Appendix A.12.</p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181991"></a><a name="_Toc153254760"></a><a
name="_Toc153254761"></a><a name="_Toc153254762"></a>3.13.4 Message Flow</h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>The ResponseToRequestReturn message is sent by a Resource Consumer
in response to an original RequestReturn message sent by the Resource Supplier.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The potential responses to this message include:</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>RequestReturn (See Section 3.12)</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span>The Supplier may send this response when the Consumer has
specified return conditions with which the Supplier is not in agreement.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet style='margin-left:0in;text-indent:0in'>The message will
typically be followed by a ReleaseResource message (See Section 3.11) when the Resource Consumer is ready to return the resource to the Resource
Supplier. </p>

<p class=MsoListBullet style='margin-left:0in;text-indent:0in'>The message may
be canceled or updated through the ResponseToRequestReturn:MessageRecall
element.</p>

<p class=MsoListBullet style='margin-left:0in;text-indent:0in'>&nbsp;</p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181992">3.13.5 Message Example</a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Below is an example of a ResponseToRequestReturn message.
This is an example response to the RequestReturn message shown in Section.3.12.5 The sender of the message is the original resource requester (Resource
Consumer). The response is an “Accept” (i.e., the Resource Consumer agrees to
return the resource according to the specified schedule). </p>

<p class=MsoListBullet style='margin-left:0in;text-indent:0in'>&nbsp;</p>

