<h2><a name="_Toc189181993"><span lang=EN>3.14 </span><span lang=EN>RequestQuote
Message</span></a></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181994"><span lang=EN>3.14.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “RequestQuote” message is used by the
Resource Consumer to request a price quote from the Resource Supplier. </span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189181995"><span lang=EN>3.14.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 14<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the RequestQuote Message. The </span><span
lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=486
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image015.jpg"></span></p>

<p class=MsoCaption><a name="_Ref153691071">Figure </a>14: EDXL-RM ERM for
RequestQuote Message</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>&nbsp;</span></p>

<span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><br clear=all
style='page-break-before:always'>
</span>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following table outlines the element cardinalities for
this message type.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=MsoCaption>Table 14: RequestQuote Message Elements </p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
