<h2><a name="_Ref150248190"></a><a name="_Toc189181999"><span lang=EN>3.15 </span><span
lang=EN>ResponseToRequestQuote</span></a><span lang=EN> Message</span></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189182000"><span lang=EN>3.15.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “ResponseToRequestQuote” message is used
by the Resource Supplier to respond to a RequestQuote Message. The supplier may
respond with pricing or decline to respond with pricing (i.e. a response that
says that the Resource Supplier is unable to supply a requested quote). The
Resource Supplier may provide quotes for several alternative resources that
match a single resource request.</span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189182001"><span lang=EN>3.15.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 15<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the ResponseToRequestQuote Message. The </span><span
lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=486
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image016.jpg"></span></p>

<p class=MsoCaption><a name="_Ref153691148">Figure </a>15: EDXL-RM ERM for
ResponseToRequestQuote Message</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>&nbsp;</span></p>

