<h2><a name="_Ref181509907"></a><a name="_Ref180289950"></a><a
name="_Toc189182005"></a><a name="_Ref188432829"></a><a name="_Ref188432765"><span
lang=EN>3.16 </span><span lang=EN>RequestResourceDeploymentStatus Message</span></a></h2>

<h3><a name="_Toc189182006"><span lang=EN>3.16.1 </span><span lang=EN>Overview</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN>The “RequestResourceDeploymentStatus” message
is used to request the current status of one or more deployed resources. It can
be sent by the Resource Supplier to the Resource Consumer (e.g., to check the
status of the resource after a “ReleaseResource” message) or by the Resource
Consumer to the Resource Supplier (e.g., to track the progress of a resource
after a “RequisitionResource” message).</span></p>

<h3><a name="_Toc189182007"><span lang=EN>3.16.2 </span><span lang=EN>Element
Reference Model</span></a></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal>Figure 16<span lang=EN> below shows the EDXL–RM Element
Reference Model (ERM) tailored for the RequestResourceDeploymentStatus Message.
The </span><span lang=EN>ERM shows the element-level details for the main
entities in the RM.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN><img border=0 width=623 height=486
src="EDXL-RM-v1.0-OS-errata-os_files/image017.jpg"></span></p>

<p class=MsoCaption><a name="_Ref153691210">Figure </a>16: EDXL-RM ERM for
RequestResourceDeploymentStatus Message</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

