 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width="15%" valign=top style='width:15.26%;background:#CCCCEE;padding:
  3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td width="84%" valign=top style='width:84.74%;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;xal:AddressType</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width="15%" valign=top style='width:15.26%;background:#CCCCEE;padding:
  3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td width="84%" valign=top style='width:84.74%;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><b>CONDITIONAL</b>, MAY be used once and only once. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width="15%" valign=top style='width:15.26%;background:#CCCCEE;padding:
  3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td width="84%" valign=top style='width:84.74%;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>A CIQ structure containing address details in an internationally-applicable
  format (See Section 1.5)</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width="15%" valign=top style='width:15.26%;background:#CCCCEE;padding:
  3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Constraints</p>
  </td>
  <td width="84%" valign=top style='width:84.74%;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>At least one of the Description, Address or TargetArea elements
  MUST be present. </p>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>An example of a CIQ AddressType can be found in section 3.10.5  </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width="98%"
 style='width:98.0%'>
 <tr>
  <td width="14%" valign=top style='width:14.98%;background:#CCCCEE;padding:
  3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><a name=ADD-targetArea><b>Element</b></a></p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>TargetArea</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>geo-oasis:WhereType</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><b>CONDITIONAL</b>, MAY be used once and only once. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>The container element for GML-based geospatial information.
  This element uses the EDXL-HAVE geo-oasis schema. It allows the target Area
  to be defined by a choice that includes:</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Constraints</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>At least one of the LocationDescription, Address or TargetArea
  elements MUST be present. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Comments</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>More detailed definitions for geo-oasis:WhereType and its
  components can be found in the geo-oasis schema. Specific usage of those
  types for EDXL-RM are found in section 4.1.13.2.1.</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<h5><a name="_Toc189182046"></a><a name="_Ref188808869">4.1.13.2.1 Imported
Type Definitions</a></h5>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width="98%"
 style='width:98.0%'>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>geo-oasis:WhereType </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Used for as the type value for TargetArea elements</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>WhereType provides a mechanism for defining location. This
  element uses the EDXL-HAVE geo-oasis schema. It allows the target Area to be
  defined as a choice of one of the following:</p>
  <ul style='margin-top:0in' type=disc>
   <li class=MsoNormal>gml:Point – WGS84 latitude and longitude</li>
   <li class=MsoNormal>gml:LineString – a series of points</li>
   <li class=MsoNormal>gml:CircleByCenterPoint – a point and radius</li>
   <li class=MsoNormal>gml:Polygon – a set of connected non-crossing lines</li>
   <li class=MsoNormal>gml:Envelope – two points used to define a bounding
       rectangle</li>
  </ul>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:12.0pt'>It also allows the use of a set
  of attributes (geo-oasis:whereAttrGroup) defined for “WhereType.” More
  detailed definitions for geo-oasis:WhereType can be found in the geo-oasis schema
  </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Comments</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>EDXL-RM uses the geo-oasis schema that is specified as an element
  of EDXL-HAVE, Both EDXL-RM and EDXL-HAVE require the use of the WGS84
  coordinate reference system.</p>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
  margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>&nbsp;</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width="98%"
 style='width:98.0%'>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>geo-oasis:WhereType using gml:Point</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Where TargetAreaType is best represented as a WGS84 point.</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>The use of gml:Point within TargetArea provides location
  using a specific WGS84 point value that is compatible with GML compliant
  geospatial information systems. The following example applies:</p>
  <pre style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:
  .5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Arial Unicode MS","sans-serif"'>         </span></strong><strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>&lt;gml:Point&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>         &lt;gml:pos&gt;45.256 -71.92&lt;/gml:pos&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>    &lt;/gml:Point&gt;</span></strong><strong><span
  style='font-family:"Arial Unicode MS","sans-serif";font-weight:normal'>    </span></strong></pre>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:12.0pt'>More detailed definitions for geo-oasis:WhereType
  can be found in the geo-oasis schema. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Constraints</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>WGS84 MUST be used for  EDXL-RM. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Requirements Supported</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
  margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>&nbsp;</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width="98%"
 style='width:98.0%'>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>geo-oasis:WhereType using gml:LineString</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Where TargetAreaType is best represented as a route along
  a series of WGS84 points. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>The use of gml:LineString within TargetArea provides
  location along a line represented by a specific list of WGS84 point values
  that is compatible with GML compliant geospatial information systems. The
  following example applies:</p>
  <pre style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:
  .5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Arial Unicode MS","sans-serif"'>      </span></strong><strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>&lt;gml:LineString&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>      &lt;gml:posList&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>         <strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>45.256 -110.45 </span></strong></span></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>         46.46 -109.48 </span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>         43.84 -109.86</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>      <strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>&lt;/gml:posList&gt;</span></strong></span></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>   &lt;/gml:LineString&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-right:.5in'><strong><span style='font-family:"Arial Unicode MS","sans-serif"'>   </span></strong>More detailed definitions for geo-oasis:WhereType can be found in the geo-oasis schema. </pre></td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Constraints</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>WGS84 MUST be used for  EDXL-RM. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Requirements Supported</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
  margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>&nbsp;</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width="98%"
 style='width:98.0%'>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>geo-oasis:WhereType using gml:CircleByCenterPoint</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Where TargetAreaType is best represented circular area of a
  given radius in kilometers around a center point represented in WGS84. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>The use of gml:CircleByCenterPoint within TargetArea
  provides location as a circle centered on a WGS84 referenced point with a
  radius defined in kilometers. The following example applies:</p>
  <pre style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:
  .5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Arial Unicode MS","sans-serif"'>      </span></strong><strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>&lt;gml:CircleByCenterPoint&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>      &lt;gml:pos&gt; 45.256 -110.45 &lt;/gml:pos&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>      &lt;gml:radius&gt; 10 &lt;/gml:radius&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>   &lt;gml:CircleByCenterPoint&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'>&nbsp;</pre>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:12.0pt'>More detailed definitions for geo-oasis:WhereType
  can be found in the geo-oasis schema. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Constraints</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>WGS84 MUST be used for EDXL-RM. </p>
  <p class=MsoListBullet><span style='font-family:Symbol'>·<span
  style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
  </span></span>For EDXL-RM the unit of measure MUST be kilometers.</p>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
  margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>&nbsp;</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width="98%"
 style='width:98.0%'>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Type</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>geo-oasis:WhereType using gml:Polygon</p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Usage</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Where TargetAreaType is best represented as a connected
  group of WGS84 points representing an actual area of concern. </p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td valign=top style='background:#CCCCEE;padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>Definition</p>
  </td>
  <td style='padding:3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt 3.0pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal>The use of gml:Polygon within TargetArea provides a ring
  of points (first and last point are the same) represented by a specific list
  of WGS84 point values that is compatible with GML compliant geospatial
  information systems. The following example applies:</p>
  <pre style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:
  .5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>&nbsp;</pre><pre style='margin-top:0in;
  margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'>      <strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>&lt;gml:Polygon&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>      &lt;gml:exterior&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>         &lt;gml:LinearRing&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>            &lt;gml:posList&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>             <strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>45.256 -110.45 </span></strong></span></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>             46.46 -109.48 </span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>             43.84 -109.86</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>             45.256 -110.45</span></strong></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>            <strong><span
  style='font-family:"Courier New";font-weight:normal'>&lt;/gml:posList&gt;</span></strong></span></pre><pre
  style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:.5in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
  margin-bottom:.0001pt'><strong><span style='font-family:"Courier New";
  font-weight:normal'>         &lt;/gml:LinearRing&gt;</span></strong></pre><pre
